# The test groups that each changed path of a pull request needs (scripts/changed-groups.sh).
# A line is a shell pattern, in which * also matches /, and the groups it needs; a pattern alone
# needs none. The checks job runs for every change, so a change that needs no group runs the
# checks alone. The first line that matches a path decides, so a narrow pattern comes before a
# wide one. A path that no line matches needs every group.
#
# packages  the version order, the packages of both programs, their tests on every system and
#           CPU type, and the lifecycle test (ci.yml)
# install   the setup script run on every system and on FreeBSD (install-tests.yml)

# What is packaged, how, and how it is tested.
programs/*                          packages install
packaging/*                         packages install
scripts/*                           packages install
Makefile                            packages install
# The lifecycle and user mode tests run the manual steps.
steps/*                             packages install
# The lifecycle test runs the setup script built from the template.
setup.sh.in                         packages install
# The release archives are proven with the published key before they are packaged.
keys/*                              packages install
# No test reads the pull request template or the settings of the dependency bot.
.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md
.github/dependabot.yml
.github/*                           packages install
# The install tests and the systems they run on.
tests/*                             install
# Read by make check alone, or by no test.
site/*
*.md
LICENSE
.gitignore
.shellcheckrc
sonar-project.properties
